  "content": "Open self-service service\n\nEndpoint: https://grf-authority.politecoast-1d7eef92.eastus.azurecontainerapps.io\nPublic protocol: HTTPS /v1/enroll, /v1/renew, /v1/register and /v1/admission. Readiness: /healthz.\n\nUse grf_starter.py init TARGET --intent \"A concrete goal\" --cloud, or grf_enroll.py TARGET. No browser signup or manual operator action is necessary. Client secrets are locally generated and kept in TARGET/credentials. Enrollment is reusable only with its original secret; knowing an account identifier or credential hash is not sufficient authentication.\n\nPublic users may register their own action hashes only within their assigned project. They cannot select owner/private policy, obtain server source, or access other accounts. This is open cooperative admission, not an independent command-safety approval service.\n\nThe service holds credential hashes, enabled flags and expiry in durable Azure Table storage. Transient action/grant state is memory-only and cleared on restart. No command text or local output is sent. Platform metadata remains outside the no-payload-logging claim.\n\nExisting mTLS/Relay mode remains supported separately. Its operator supplies unique client certificate/project/policy and Send-only Relay credentials. Keep local private keys local. Legacy Relay mode requires: python -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-relay.txt\n\nNo owner/admin credentials, CA signing keys, Listen/Manage credentials or private implementation are distributed.\n"
}
